# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit real values.
# This repository and its agent session logs (.claude-logs/) are PUBLIC: never paste a real key
# into a prompt, a doc, a test or a commit. Placeholders must not look like real keys.
# Local values: run `pnpm db:start` then `pnpm exec supabase status`.

# --- Public (exposed to browser) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Server only ---
# Bypasses RLS. Only used by src/lib/supabase/admin.ts.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Optional: send invitation emails via Resend (D13). Leave unset to skip email.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_…
# EMAIL_FROM=Jarso <hello@example.com>

# Optional: the AI money guide (ADR 0010). Off unless FEATURE_GUIDE=true and a key is set.
# The key is a server secret: set it in Vercel (Production) and, for evals, as a GitHub
# repository secret. Never in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, a doc, a test or a chat.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-…
# FEATURE_GUIDE=false
# GUIDE_DAILY_BUDGET_CENTS=1000
# GUIDE_MONTHLY_BUDGET_CENTS=10000
# GUIDE_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Optional: card handover payments (test mode only). A provider is on when all its keys are set,
# and several can be on at once (the parent picks one). A provider with only some of its keys
# stays off and the server logs which names are missing. The fake provider is for tests and local
# runs: PAYMENTS_ALLOW_FAKE=true turns it on, never on Vercel production.
# The keys are server secrets: set them in Vercel and never in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable or a chat.
# PAYMENTS_ALLOW_FAKE=false
# Stripe (test mode keys only):
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_…
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_…
# Razorpay (test mode only: the key id must start rzp_test_; INR families only):
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_…
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=replace-with-the-test-key-secret
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=replace-with-the-dashboard-webhook-secret

# Cron routes (Vercel Cron and the pg_cron job via pg_net) send "Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>".
# At least 16 characters; unset turns the cron routes off (404). Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string

# Optional: web push (FR16). Make a key pair once with `pnpm exec web-push generate-vapid-keys`.
# The public key is safe in the browser; the private key is a server secret:
# set it in Vercel (Production, sensitive). Unset means push is skipped and the inbox still works.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=B…
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=…
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:hello@example.com
